    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Let me summarize what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `salutation` feature to the owner endpoints. The request may include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the owner's `salutation` is derived as `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nFollowing the codebase's existing convention \u2014 store the *source* fields on the entity and *derive* presentation values in the MapStruct mapper (as done for `displayName`, `initials`, etc.) \u2014 I made these changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (source of the generated DTOs):\n   - Added `title` to `OwnerFields` (an editable input, `MR|MRS|MS|DR`), so it lands in both `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response).\n   - Added `salutation` as a read-only field on `Owner`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `title` field with getter/setter (a `title` column). MapStruct auto-maps `title` request\u2192entity and entity\u2192response by name.\n\n3. **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table so the stored title survives to the `GET` read-back.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a small `salutation(Owner)` derivation method plus its `@Mapping`, keeping the logic in a single-responsibility unit alongside the other derived fields.\n\nThe logic lives where the analogous derived fields already live (the mapper), the entity only stores the raw `title`, and no existing class grew a catch-all responsibility.\n\n**Tests:** the new `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` passes (`$.salutation` = `\"DR who\"`), and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
